# Select and copy: a drag selects text of a reply, in the chat and in the terminal; a Copy (the message's menu, ⌘C)
# puts it on the sandbox's own pasteboard (never yours); ⌘V puts it in the composer, which must then hold exactly the
# selection (`composer expect`: a difference fails the journey at that line, saying what the composer holds).
desc Drag-select a reply in the chat and the terminal, copy it (menu, ⌘C), paste it into the composer and check it.
chat
# No inspector: its clock and run values would each need a mask.
inspector hide

# The chat: the menu's Copy.
pointer drag takes schedule
shot chat-selected
pointer menu-copy takes
composer paste
composer expect takes its lock after it reads the sche
shot chat-pasted-menu
composer clear

# The chat: ⌘C (the selection is dragged again: the composer took the keyboard from the message).
pointer drag takes schedule
pointer copy
composer paste
composer expect takes its lock after it reads the sche
shot chat-pasted-key
composer clear

# The terminal: its Ready. line, dragged across from its first line's start into its second, then ⌘C.
terminal
drag
shot terminal-selected
copy
chat
composer paste
composer expect dy.
shot terminal-pasted

# What changes from run to run on its own, in the 2560x1600 shots of the main window (inspector hidden): the
# session's age in its sidebar row and in the header's state pill, and the clock time under the question.
mask *-main-* 430 250 75 45
mask *-main-* 1115 118 140 44
mask *-main-* 2300 320 100 45
